==============================================================================
S1b  The implicit force balance IS exactly linear in lumped coefficients
==============================================================================
  residual(lumped, substituted back) - residual(raw) = [0, 0, 0]
  identity holds: True
  residual is affine in every lumped coefficient (all 2nd derivatives zero): True
  number of lumped coefficients = 11 (A, B, G, MH, MD, MD2, CG1, CG2, CBs, CY, KBs)
  ADMISSIBILITY CONSTRAINTS (the embedding is exact but REDUNDANT):
    MH appears in M0[2,2], M1[0,1], M1[1,0] and M2[1,1] and must be the SAME scalar;
    MD^2 = MD2 * MH   (since MD = mh*d, MD2 = mh*d^2  =>  MD^2 = mh^2 d^2 = MH*MD2);
    A, G, MH > 0 and M(Y) > 0 over the scheduling range.
  Estimating MD and MD2 as free coefficients breaks MD^2 = MH*MD2 and leaves the
  physical (mh, d) unrecoverable; it is 11 coefficients for 10 degrees of freedom.
  VERDICT H1b: ACCEPTED with the redundancy constraint named.
  NOTE on the estimator: this residual is M(Y) times the acceleration error, so
  least squares on r weights the three logical channels by M(Y) and needs qddot.
  It is a different estimand from output prediction; see decision-report.md.

